Waterbody means any surface water of the state, as likewise defined in the Michigan Administrative Code R 323.1044(u), and includes:

(1) The Great Lakes and their connecting waters;

(2) All inland lakes;

(3) Rivers;

(4) Streams;

(5) Impoundments;

(6) Open drains;

(7) Wetlands; and

(8) Other surface bodies of water within the confines of the state. Drainage ways and ponds used solely for wastewater conveyance, treatment, or control are expressly excluded from this definition.
